# openccu-lite: the warnings the two boots of lite-qemu-test.sh may log (the ova image under QEMU, boot 1
# with its shutdown, and boot 2 on the seeded userfs). Format: scripts/lite-boot-warnings.sh. Every line
# says why the warning stays; a warning that is fixed leaves this list, so it fails when it comes back.
# Made from 1.0.0-beta.0's boot test (2026-10-10, task 345), less the lines task 345 removed at their
# cause (udev's clock group, nfs-utils' rules, dbus's user switch, tmpfiles' /root/.ssh, the lighttpd
# reload at a shutdown, lighttpd's refused loopback backends, the kernel audit records).

# --- the virtual machine (QEMU, TCG, the qemu64 CPU) ---
^kernel: tsc: Unable to calibrate against PIT$ ## QEMU's emulated timer under TCG
^kernel: mtrr: your CPUs had inconsistent (fixed|variable) MTRR settings$ ## QEMU's virtual CPUs
^kernel: mtrr: your CPUs had inconsistent MTRRdefType settings$ ## QEMU's virtual CPUs
^kernel: acpi PNP0A03:00: fail to add MMCONFIG information, can't access extended configuration space under this bridge$ ## QEMU's i440fx machine has no MMCONFIG
^kernel: hyperv_fb: Deprecated: use Hyper-V DRM driver instead$ ## the ova kernel carries the Hyper-V drivers; the driver says so at load
^kernel: amd_pstate: the _CPC object is not present in SBIOS or ACPI disabled$ ## QEMU's firmware has no CPPC tables
^systemd: Failed to open any watchdog device before the initial transaction completed: No such file or directory$ ## QEMU without a watchdog device; a VM with one, and the boards, have it
^\(udev-worker\): cpu[0-9]+: Process '/bin/sh -c '\[ -e /dev/xen/xenbus \] && \[ -e /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu[0-9]+/online \] && echo 1 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu[0-9]+/online'' failed with exit code 1\.$ ## a Xen CPU hotplug rule; its test is false outside Xen and udev reports the false test as a failure
^systemd: systemd-udevd\.service: unit configures an IP firewall, but the local system does not support BPF/cgroup firewalling\.$ ## udevd's upstream IPAddressDeny=; the kernel has no cgroup BPF firewall, and udevd needs none
^systemd: systemd-udevd\.service: \(This warning is only shown for the first unit using IP firewalling\.\)$ ## the line above's second half

# --- the kernel and the boot (every image) ---
^kernel: check access for rdinit=/init failed: -2, ignoring$ ## no initramfs; the kernel looks for one first
^kernel: eq3_char_loop: loading out-of-tree module taints kernel\.$ ## eQ-3's multiplexer module is out of tree by nature
^systemd: Dependency failed for Start psplash-systemd progress communication helper\.$ ## headless QEMU has no framebuffer, so psplash-start fails (B-130)
^lighttpd: \(\.\./src/server\.c\.[0-9]+\) reducing server\.max-connections \([0-9]+\) to 1/10 server\.max-fds \([0-9]+\)$ ## lighttpd's own notice of its fd limit (B-254), logged at warning by lighttpd
^chronyd: System clock wrong by -?[0-9.]+ seconds$ ## chronyd's makestep at the start corrects a clock that ran without NTP (no RTC, the VM's drift across the test's reboot); the size depends on timing. chronyd logs both lines at warning with no setting for it: `logchange` would quiet this one but also a later real jump, and the step line has no threshold (task 346)
^chronyd: System clock was stepped by -?[0-9.]+ seconds$ ## the line above's step
^lighttpd: \(\.\./src/server\.c\.[0-9]+\) warning: clock jumped [0-9]+ secs$ ## lighttpd notices chronyd's step above when it is large
^irqbalance: WARNING: MSI interrupts found in /proc/interrupts$ ## irqbalance's notice on a Raspberry Pi 4 whose PCIe MSIs (the VL805 USB controller) are in /proc/interrupts but have no msi_irqs/ entries in sysfs; it only means irqbalance classifies them by guess, which costs nothing on 4 cores; seen at every boot of a Pi 4 on 1.0.0-beta.2 (task 346)
^irqbalance: But none found in sysfs, you need to update your kernel$ ## the line above's second line
^irqbalance: Until then, IRQs will be improperly classified$ ## the line above's third line

# --- occulited (its levels are occulited's: rows 7 and 11 of task 345 are occulited task 34) ---
^occulited: no users yet: the web UI asks for the administrator password on first visit$ ## a fresh image has no account by design
^occulited: rpc: interface down interface=[A-Za-z-]+ err="HTTP request failed on 127\.0\.0\.1:[0-9]+[^ ]*: .*(dial tcp 127\.0\.0\.1:[0-9]+: connect: connection refused|read tcp 127\.0\.0\.1:[0-9]+->127\.0\.0\.1:[0-9]+: read: connection reset by peer)" retry_in=[0-9]+s$ ## occulited starts before the interface daemons (occulited task 34): refused while the daemon is not up yet, or reset when it goes down while occulited's request is in flight - boot 2's rfd, which fails without its seeded gateway, timing-dependent (B-323)
^occulited: rpc: deregistration failed interface=[A-Za-z-]+ err= ## occulited stops after the interface daemons (occulited task 34)
^occulited: boot timeline: this boot could not be read err="systemctl show: context (deadline exceeded|canceled)"$ ## systemctl answers slowly under TCG on a loaded runner, or the shutdown cancels the read; occulited reports the helper socket's read deadline as the context's since occulited B-71 (B-323 had allowed its i/o timeout form)

# --- hmipserver ---
^hmipserver: de\.eq3\.lib\.measurement\.MeasurementService \[[^]]+\] The configuration file path "(/etc/config|/opt/HMServer)/measurement" doen't exist or is not a directory\.$ ## the diagram feature without its configuration (occulited tasks 32, 33)
^hmipserver: io\.vertx\.core\.impl\.BlockedThreadChecker \[vertx-blocked-thread-checker\] Thread Thread\[#[0-9]+,vert\.x-eventloop-thread-[0-9]+,[0-9]+,main\] has been blocked for [0-9]+ ms, time limit is [0-9]+ ms$ ## hmipserver's event loop is slow under TCG while occulited's init runs (B-270's shape)
^hmipserver: io\.vertx\.core\.VertxException: Thread blocked$ ## the line above's exception
^hmipserver: de\.eq3\.cbcs\.server\.core\.vertx\.KeyServerWorker \[[^]]+\] Missing or invalid key server configuration parameter ## the key server mode without its network key (occulited B-63)

# --- what the test itself provokes ---
^systemd: lighttpd\.service: Main process exited, code=killed, status=9/KILL$ ## the test kills lighttpd to see the unit restart it
^systemd: lighttpd\.service: Failed with result 'signal'\.$ ## the same kill
^systemd: Failed to start crond\.service\.$ ## boot 2: the test masks crond through unit-switch.json
^rfd: UnifiedLanCommController::connect\(\): Unable to connect\.$ ## boot 2: the test seeds an unreachable LAN gateway
^rfd: CCU2LGWCommController::init\(\): Cannot connect to HomeMatic Lan Gateway with serial number KEQ0123456\.$ ## boot 2: the seeded gateway
^rfd: No BidCoS-Interface available$ ## boot 2: the seeded gateway is rfd's only interface
^systemd: rfd\.service: Failed with result 'exit-code'\.$ ## boot 2: rfd without its seeded gateway
^systemd: Failed to start BidCos-RF Interface\.$ ## boot 2: the same
^hmipserver: de\.eq3\.ccu\.bidcos\.dispatcher\.BidCosRpcDispatcher \[[^]]+\] (BidCosCache could not be initialized|java\.net\.ConnectException: Connection refused|Could not register BidCos-RF_java)$ ## boot 2: rfd is down without its seeded gateway
^hm2mqtt: no MQTT broker configured - open Systemsteuerung -> hm2mqtt$ ## boot 1: the test installs hm2mqtt from the catalogue without a broker; the addon says so at warning
^node-red: openccu-lite: the Node-RED editor signs in with the box session from the X-Occulite-Session header$ ## boot 1: the test installs RedMatic from the catalogue; RedMatic logs its session sign-in at warning
^systemd: addon-redmatic\.service: Failed with result 'exit-code'\.$ ## boot 1: the test uninstalls RedMatic seconds after its start, and RedMatic's stop exits non-zero while Node-RED still starts
^occulited: addon supervisor: the addon's daemon ended, restarting its unit addon=hm2mqtt unit=addon-hm2mqtt\.service attempt=[0-9]+$ ## boot 1: the test's hm2mqtt has no broker, its daemon ends and the supervisor restarts it until the test uninstalls it (timing: before or after the uninstall)
